## 10. Splunk Integration

Business handlers must not contain direct Splunk-specific implementation.

Avoid:

```csharp
await splunkClient.SendAsync(...);
```

inside every handler.

Prefer:

```text
Business Handler
      |
      v
IAuditService
      |
      v
Common Audit Framework
      |
      v
Standardized Audit Event
      |
      v
Central Logging / Splunk Integration
```

The business application should depend on an abstraction such as `IAuditService`.

The framework owns event creation, schema consistency, serialization, correlation metadata, validation, and destination integration.

Keep the destination implementation replaceable.

If the existing enterprise architecture uses CloudWatch -> Splunk, preserve it rather than introducing a direct Splunk SDK dependency.

