# Final Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is acceptable only when:

- Multiple independent .NET 10 applications can consume the same audit framework.
- Every application produces the same canonical audit schema.
- Every record-level action produces a traceable audit event.
- UI/API and Step Functions actions are distinguishable.
- `recordId`, `operationId`, `correlationId`, and workflow execution information can be correlated.
- Success and failure are clearly represented.
- Retries are distinguishable from duplicate business operations.
- Sensitive information is not logged.
- Business logic remains isolated from Splunk implementation details.
- The framework is compatible with VSA + Clean Architecture.
- The framework is suitable for high-volume processing.
- The audit contract is protected by automated contract tests.
- Existing functionality continues to work.

